@KILLERTIGER
! Micah comes back, don't worry. You'll get to see him a few times!

Hi
@QuikInk
! You're lucky number...last? I'm going to be tweaking a few things, waiting for a bit more feedback from playtesters (find the bugs! Find them all!) then I'll be putting out a public demo. You are welcome to playtest this version, and I'll message you the download, just be aware a modified version is coming soon!

@Kupotepo
Sure, let me know if you remember the enemy. Also, Ella's Steal does inflict low damage; you can upgrade it to do more damage, and then have a chance to Confuse. It's not a damaging move, but I will consider adding another bonus to it to make the skill feel more rewarding in combat.
Thanks, I'm glad you're enjoying the story!
@KILLERTIGER
Thank you, I'll take a look through the mines and see where the passable error is.

Thanks
@Kupotepo
! Those have actually been fixed, but I didn't feel some passable issues warranted a whole game update haha. All the goodies in the storage shed are on the other shelves, so if choose to steal from the poor town even after the guy asked you not to take any of the limited supplies, you aren't missing anything

@ShadowDragon
Yay! I hope Cerbie was just a difficult fight and wasn't unbalanced. Also, he won't be the hardest fight for very long... :3
I have fixed all the grammar+tileset issues you've sent me haha. Out of curiosity...did you get the hidden achievement after Cerbie?

@Cythera
Correction, lv 13 for beating Cerbie at lowest level possible
but lv 16 or higher is recommended for Cerbie

This is a puzzle you solved in kindergarten?  Well, then, I feel really stupid because I can't even figure out the gist of the puzzle!   We'll see how
@kimo
makes out.  At least if I do go back, it's really not that far back.  I hate missing out on a legendary piece of equipment.

@Lady_JJ
It's on... sometimes really smart people like you can overthink a puzzle that us simple-minded ones can easily solve. And sometimes I can put my whole foot in my mouth.
@ShadowDragon
I agree that dying 50x is indeed the easiest Accomplishment in this game. And, yeah, the reward for the whole party remaining alive during a boss battle should be something you cannot get anywhere else in the game.
@Cythera
My rubber mallet (dispells confusion) is missing from inventory. Did you steal it by making it consumable in the update? Or is there a limit to its uses?
I got an "itch" this morning that I had to scratch.

@ShadowDragon
I don't know/remember who Lyla is. But now you have me thinking. LVL 12? I hadn't figured out the Monster form and spells at Lvl 12. This is a very complex game that makes replays highly likely for most players.
@Cythera
What does ProcRate mean for crafted armor?
Anyone have suggestions on what crafting books to buy in Trader's Fort? There are a load of them including an advanced weapon book that doesn't seem to allow any crafting of advanced weapons at this point in the game. There are way too many books, augments, etc. in this town to buy them all.

@ShadowDragon
- I went back to a previous save and my characters are level 12.  I suspect I explored a bit more around the Highlands before attempting Lyla, but I did load that save and headed straight there.  Uh, yeah, I couldn't keep everyone alive.  Ella, in particular, seemed to be very vulnerable to Lyla's spells.  I do have some copper and iron I could try crafting into more resistant state armors, but I'm not sure I have the patience for it.  I'm thinking you're going to be one of the few, if not the only, player to be successful at that level.
@Cythera
- I'm still stuck on that number puzzle.  I wondered why I didn't remember that solving it gained a legendary item.  I went back to a previous save (fortunately had one just prior to the jump into the sandpool) and now I know how I missed it.  The directions to the puzzle and the reward are only shown the first time you read that northern wall.  Then you have to solve the first two puzzles, so by the time you need that information, unless you've written down all those directions the first time, they're never shown to you again.  I think you should consider giving an option to reread those directions so people can focus in on them after the first two gates are lifted.  I wrote the directions down and saved them.  Perhaps they'll make sense in my next lifetime, but at least I can reread them.  Here's what I don't understand...
Spoiler
The top line is 00000765.  The hint is that there is one 4.  According to the directions, that means I put a 1 above the 4 and a 4 above the 1, so now the top line is 04001675.  The 765 seems to fulfill the condition of 5 7's, so 5 above the 7 and 7 above the 5, and 6 6's so 6 over 6.  That only leaves a few other possibilities: 04231675, 04321675, 24031675, 34201675, all of which satisfy the conditions, so what in the directions am I missing?

@Lady_JJ
I think the other choice for "hiding" was "from the Pirates". Did the girl mention the pirates after Vincent left? Another choice for one conversation branch is Vincent asking the girl if she would like to join the party. She is flattered, but refuses. Does she act later on any of these choices? Hmmmmmmm. A very complicated branch that would provide all kinds of future options (and programming nightmares for
@Cythera
).
I agree with your comment about any major reward. It's what most players would expect, not just us. I may not be a fan of all the boxes sometimes, but all too often I have had to look for "new" in the inventory list to see what I recently obtained.
@ShadowDragon
I break games by going places no one thought about or "out of sequence" from what the developer thought a player would typically do. I have no idea what "glitch" you found, but keep it up because that is what any developer needs to know if they want to be the world's best
robot maker
game designer.

@kimo
Spoiler
I just go for the latest ore and spend a lot of time rolling for bloodthirsty and regen traits.  You'll get lots more gems as drops soon.  I tend to go for the gloves first, just because they can hold augments.

@ShadowDragon
Those relationship setting are only under Victor's Status>Combat guide heading. Those Vincent/Mara exchanges often make me laugh because they are sooooooooo real.
@Cythera
Did you notice
@ShadowDragon
found some of those "features" you were telling me about?
I change my FPS lock rate in the game per your advice. While it seems enemies may not be running around as fast, I can still replicate being trapped in any corner if there is only 1 direction in which to escape. The enemy flames just do not disappear after being defeated, so my party is unable to escape through the enemy occupied square.
I made a copy of the save file for you if you are interested. This is exactly the same issue as I reported before when I was trapped in the SE corner of the "Southern route map?" before the village. Sorry, but I have forgotten the name of the village.

@Cythera
,
@kimo
,
@Lady_JJ
did you got this hardcore? (im currently lv 42-43
so far with my team: ))4rd hardcore on the road.
What feature did you tlk about
@kimo
?.  if you talk about enemy respawn, some
spawn faster, but it is also possible that they respawn, while the timer continue even
when you are in the menu?
because the time played also keep ticking in the menu and doesn't pause this.

@ShadowDragon
I only have Cerbie and Presipa. You 2 are way ahead of me. The "feature" I was talking about was Vincent being able to walk on the stovetop.
@Cythera
called it a "feature" (not a mapping issue) and I was joking about it to her.
@Lady_JJ
I'm not sure what square you are talking about in the Temple of Fire. Sounds like a cook trick. But, my problem has been that I have been trapped in 2 different corners by a flame that never goes away. Lucky I had a very recent save.

@ShadowDragon
Spoiler
Remember when you played as Micah the second time? And he and Cadriel beat up Asher? Yah, Asher was obviously carrying some Relics with him then, and Cecilia took them at the point
@Lady_JJ
Uhhhhhh. Whelp. I'm off to find out why the level cap can be bypassed! XD
@kimo
Noooo, fire is strong against ice; you just cut Vincent's damage output in half with the ice augment against fire enemies haha! And passives are visible in character status -> profile outside of combat as well. I'll send you a message regarding the save file.

@Cythera
Thanks, now I understand the Elemental Data arrows. I gave him Light instead.
I cannot find where the learned Passives would be in the status variables. Attributes seems to be the closest, but the passive aspects are not identified as such. What am I missing?

@Cythera
- I think I didn't start a completely new game with verison 2.x.  If the level cap wasn't present in 1.2, maybe that's why I was able to climb above?
@kimo
- I got my temples mixed up.  The puzzle was in the temple to the north, where the village kids were trapped.

Lady_JJ said:
@kimo - I don't think anyone in your party has the time or the inclination to take up a hobby like rock collecting. Maybe someone else in town would be interested, though? Maybe someone just hanging around playing pick up sticks?
Click to expand...
I've been back to her but apparently I don't have enough stones yet. I've looked everywhere, but
@Cythera
apparently has researched Indy's approach to quest design. I think we are in trouble.

Okay. I give. How the #%$ do you cause damage to the Watcher. I am obviously doing something wrong or am improperly equipped since both
@Lady_JJ
and
@ShadowDragon
have both beaten this sucker.
I can get it down about 8-9k HP below its max but then the critter keeps absorbing and regenerating HP and I cannot do enough damage either in Vincent or Monster mode or with any spells. I believe the problem is being caused when The Watcher casts Polish. It took me forever to find the "right" sandpool and now it looks like I need another lifetime to ever beat this thing.

The lockpick-So, I've tried and tried, but, nope.  No way can I do it. Sometimes I get a lucky one that has 3 or 4 of the same symbol in a row, so I can get to the last 2, but that's it.  I want to know more about Squall's 'hidden room' that
@ShadowDragon
is exploring...
@Cythera
- the omagan is a fairly easy battle, I'm assuming because it's just a baby.  Can it be diverted or is killing it the only option?

@ShadowDragon
- I misunderstood your comment then.  I thought you meant there was a secret room somewhere near there.  As for the lockpick, there is no way I am ever going to be able to do it.  The time it takes me to process what the next key is and then direct the correct finger to press just takes too long.  Slowing reflexes is just a consequence of the aging process.  I could do the earlier lockpick because the sequence was hard coded.  I just wrote down U_L_D_ (or whatever it was) and that was easier for me.  Looking at the symbol, then having to interpret that symbol, adds a middle step for mental processing and that makes this puzzle impossible for me.  I do appreciate you telling what's in there, though.  It looks like there's little there that I can't farm elsewhere.  When you say dark crystal, do you mean dark mana?
@Cythera
- Will this next release complete the story then?  As impatient as I am for the story to continue, please do take your time.  It is apparent that you have put your heart and soul into this game.  It is nearly perfect.  One of the best games I've played in a long time.  If there's only about 5 hours of play left, then I'll probably finish the game first as an avid fan, then restart a fresh game as a playtester.

@ShadowDragon
- That's a nice offer and I do thank you.  I won't take you up on it this time, but maybe when I do a runthrough of the final released game.
At the moment, I don't need any more dark mana.  I still have 18 in reserve and all players have attained their passives.  I spent some time farming dark mana and ethane minerals back in the Eastern Forest before entering the Basalt Mines.

@ShadowDragon
I like your idea of a sliding scale of reward for the supply room. After all, I paid 1 Mana Stone to find out the 1st clock number for that puzzle. So also skipping the lock by paying some mana stones would work for anyone I think. Dark Mana stones should not be given if the player cannot pick the lock as
@Cythera
wants them to do.
It's really a matter of whether the game will sell very well to the players that will love the story, if they have trouble with tasks that are too challenging because of the players' lack of dexterity, vision challenges, etc.
I missed the statue carvings and will go back when
@Cythera
releases the next part. See you then.

@ShadowDragon
A longer time length for picking the lock would be preferable to me, but if
@Cythera
wants to retain the current time length to accomplish the task, I suggested Mana stones because they have serious value. I did omit "Dark" from mana stones. And, of course, those Dark Mana stones might not be found inside the storge room.
But your other suggestions are valid options, too.
I just always think players with some physical limitation should never be "locked out" of any quest/task/game sequences after reading many years of comments from those people. It's like me with red/green situations.

I am not sleeping,
@ShadowDragon
! I am not! I am - Im literally laying in bed right now ._.
Okay, so I took a step back recently haha. I also just finished about 30 maps; be nice
Nice catch,
@Lady_JJ
thanks! I fixed it with some region restrictions. On one level you need to walk behind the cables to get a treasure chest, hence the star pass ability ^-^
Awesome,
@hdhayes11
! There is a demo available right now that has roughly 27-30 hours of gameplay. I'd love to hear your feedback on my game

@hdhayes11
Definitely download the game and start playing. I'm going to be playing this a second time after the game is completed. Just ignore any typos/grammar errors for now. I checked and
@Cythera
did pass High School English .... Remedial(?).
3 of us have been playing this game for a few weeks and finding minor issues. No one has been stuck while playing this game. It is certainly a challenging game and I'm sure a person with a new view would help
@Cythera
make some design decisions. She takes critiques rather well (at least I have never seen her cry about anything).
@Cythera
The lockpick sequence is, of course, your decision. My previous comment about giving up precious Dark Mana Stones, but not finding any inside the room, is still a decent option for people who value equipment over skills. However, I think extending the time allotment until
@Lady_JJ
can finish the task is a good choice too; maybe even better because it would give a feeling of completion without a compromise being made.
I'm really looking forward to your next release version.

@Cythera
- I think you should not be coerced into changing the lockpick sequence.  As long as it opens the door to a non-essential main quest area, then that's perfectly fair.  The way it's set up now, I know I can't complete the task, but I also know I can farm dark mana and crafting items elsewhere, so it's all good.  And knowing someone will 'spill the beans' to let me know what I missed out on (giving a nod and a wink to
@kimo
and
@ShadowDragon
here) is enough to fulfill the completionist in me.  Now, if that doorway led to the next chapter in the game and my slow reflexes prevented me from continuing the game, that would be a totally different issue.  I think if you nerfed it down so that 'even an old lady' could complete it, then it wouldn't be a challenge at all.  But I do think
@kimo
should be able to complete it, so maybe a small time extension?
30 more maps!!!  WOOHOO!!  I'm so looking forward to continuing this wonderful saga.
@hdhayes11
- please do as
@kimo
suggested and start playing.  I know I sound like a broken record (now you see just how very old I really am), but this is absolutely one of the best games I've played in a long, long time.

@Lady_JJ
You did better than I did with that last lock picking. Now who's old? The trick is not spending time translating the symbol into the necessary action which apparently you and I both had done. As long as the lockpicking sequence is not randomized, there is the chance to memorize the sequence and accomplish the task.
@Cythera
Here's a thought to ponder. When learning how to design tests, there is one basic statistic you are taught. A "good" question is one that 50% get right and 50% get wrong and the ones who get it right have the higher overall test scores. It follows that if the 50% who get the question right were in the bottom percentiles, the question is "bad". So could you have a "test group" just on this singular game task and see what the outcome is? A simple ratio of 50/50 might be enough given the challenge despite the variables that would not be possible to address. (i.e. everyone in the group is under a specific age with a high dexterity). Just a thought.

@kimo
loving that you're pruning your fruit trees and bottling your own wine, all while test driving RPG's. It's an eclectic life you have.
@ShadowDragon
so there was another game a few years ago that I really liked a lot but I couldn't get past a snowball-chasing-you-down-the-mountain minievent.  Unfortunately this was a QTE that was critical to the main quest, so truly a game stopper if it couldn't be done.  I made a list of each keypress (left x 3, down x 2, right x 7, etc.) and coded a program (using BASIC, not javascript) to simulate keypresses.  It was the only way I could get past this.  (The developer was adamant that he wanted his game to remain hard and there was no way he would nerf this particular event.)  But that was an event with a known sequence of keypresses.  I've since modified it on a couple of occasions to get past similar timed events.  But, I'm wondering, just how would you do it for a random sequence?  I know you said you wouldn't share it, and I'm not asking for details, just (yes or no) is there a way the software can detect those random symbols.  That would be well over my coding ability.  I'm just glad it wasn't a game stopper.
@Cythera
We'll wait (im)patiently because it's important that the game remain fun for you and not become an unnecessary drudgery.  But, if you have the motivation to speed things up, well, you know....

@Lady_JJ
Yep, but I have worked my butt of in life and made many personal sacrifices to get to a point where I can do what makes me happy. I am also easily bored, so eclectic is virtually a way of life for me. Hmmmm, maybe that's why my furniture doesn't match? I'm always up for learning something I never knew before.
@Cythera
I'm not a gaming slut, but I just ran into one of those QTE situations in another game on this site. At the risk of you implementing the idea, the thief character has to complete a 3-4 arrow sequence to be successful at stealing from the enemy. Another NPC has an intense "Uppercut" move that requires a similar sequence to suceed in the skill.
Don't worry. Politics is completely off the table, because as Ron White says, "You can't fix stupid...".

@Cythera
Okay, crystals are done. Thank you. I think the confusion comes from the fact that wall tile count is used as the decision basis, but the clue just says "Walls". To me, individual tiles do not equal individual walls. I was overthinking the challenge.
It's really more of a horizontal wall width function, so the wall width North (above?) of each crystal is what a player needs to calculate. Also, each wall tile is "1-step" wide. These are just some random thoughts for making it more clear in the hint given.

@Lady_JJ
I know you keep great notes, so where is the Dragon Gear Book? I have found the Gold book, but where did I miss that one? I'm in the Mossbank River area, so I may be too late.
@Cythera
If you create a guide for this game, I would suggest you make a note for players of what level they should be as they make major advances in the game. I luckily had a save in Mossbank to where I just restarted. I was only level 20 when facing Presipa and kept getting my butt kicked in Nalia's Gift area.

@Cythera
So happy to see you're back and that you're feeling less stressed. I've been playing a new game of Indy's on his Aldorlea site (so has
@Lady_JJ
). I'll be back soon. I just wanted to say "Aloha".
